 Sure! Here's a PHP custom function named `smart_sort_array` that meets your requirements:

```php
function smart_sort_array($set, $order = 'ASC') { // Order can be either ASC or DESC
    if (!is_array($set) || count($set) <= 1) {
        return $set; // Return the input array if it's empty or contains only one element
    }

    for ($i = 0; $i < count($set) - 1; $i++) {
        for ($j = $i + 1; $j < count($set); $j++) {
            if (($order === 'ASC' && $set[$i]['age'] > $set[$j]['age']) || ($order === 'DESC' && $set[$i]['age'] < $set[$j]['age'])) {
                // Swap the positions of i and j elements
                $temp = $set[$i];
                $set[$i] = $set[$j];
                $set[$j] = $temp;
            }
        }
    }

    return $set;
}
```

This function accepts two parameters: `$set`, which is the main array containing sub-arrays, and `$order`, which is the order parameter with default value 'ASC'. It checks if the input array is valid and then sorts the array using simple switching of elements based on the provided order.

 I'm here to help you write code! Based on your description, it sounds like you're looking for a function that takes an object (represented as a string in dot notation) and returns all entries from an array of objects where a specific nested property matches the given key. Here's an example implementation:

```javascript
function findNestedObject(obj, key) {
  let parts = key.split(".");
  let current = obj;

  for (let i = 0; i < parts.length; i++) {
    if (!current || !current[parts[i]]) {
      return null;
    }
    current = current[parts[i]];
  }

  return current;
}

function findObjectsWithKey(arr, key) {
  return arr.filter((obj) => {
    const nestedValue = findNestedObject(obj, key);
    return nestedValue !== undefined;
  });
}

// Usage
const data = [
  {
    a: { b: "foo" },
    c: { d: "bar" },
  },
  {
    a: { b: "qux" },
  },
];

const result = findObjectsWithKey(data, "a.b"); // [{ a: { b: 'foo' }}]
```

This code defines two functions: `findNestedObject` and `findObjectsWithKey`. The `findNestedObject` function recursively navigates through an object using dot notation keys until it reaches the target property or encounters a null value. The `findObjectsWithKey` function uses `findNestedObject` to filter an array of objects and return only those that have the specified nested property with the matching value.

