 To create a simple toast notification using React and the useContextHook, follow these steps:

First, let's create a custom context provider for managing the toast messages and displaying them as notifications.

1. Create a new file called `ToastContext.js`:

```javascript
import { createContext, useState } from 'react';

export const ToastContext = createContext();

export const ToastProvider = ({ children }) => {
  const [toasts, setToasts] = useState([]);

  const addToast = (message) => {
    setToasts((prevToasts) => [...prevToasts, message]);
  };

  return (
    <ToastContext.Provider value={{ toasts, addToast }}>
      {children}
      <div id="toast-container" className="fixed bottom-0 right-0 p-6 w-full max-w-xs">
        {toasts.map((toast, index) => (
          <div key={index} className="bg-white border border-gray-300 text-gray-500 px-4 py-3 rounded shadow-md mb-4">
            {toast}
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </ToastContext.Provider>
  );
};
```

2. Wrap your application with the `ToastProvider`. Add this wrapper component around your `App` or main component in your `index.js` file:

```javascript
// index.js
import React from 'react';
import ReactDOM from 'react-dom';
import App from './App';
import ToastProvider from './ToastContext';

ReactDOM.render(
  <React.StrictMode>
    <ToastProvider>
      <App />
    </ToastProvider>
  </React.StrictMode>,
  document.getElementById('root')
);
```

