Here's an example SQL code snippet that includes error handling and data validation:

```sql
CREATE PROCEDURE ConvertTemperature
    @Celsius DECIMAL(5,2),
    @Output FLOAT OUTPUT
AS
BEGIN
    SET NOCOUNT ON;

    -- Check if input value is valid
    IF @Celsius IS NULL OR @Celsius < -273.15 OR @Celsius > 500 THB
    BEGIN
        SET @Output = -1;
        RAISERROR('Invalid Celsius value.', 16, 1);
        RETURN;
    END;

    -- Convert Celsius to Fahrenheit
    SET @Fahrenheit = (@Celsius * 1.8) + 32;
    SET @Output = CAST(@Fahrenheit AS FLOAT);
END;
GO;
```

This stored procedure checks if the input Celsius value is within the valid range before performing the temperature conversion and returns an error message and a -1 output value if it is not.

